<title>JAPAN: Honda falls on report of possible lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Honda falls on report of possible lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Honda Motor Co Ltd tumbled on Friday on a foreign wire service report that more than 60 of its auto dealers will request a judge in Baltimore to grant class-action status for lawsuits claiming Honda gave more of its best-selling models to dealerships that bribed executives.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the car maker was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>As of 0515 GMT, the shares were down 250 yen or 6.75 percent at 3,450, making Honda the fifth largest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
</text>
